1. ggml and llama.cpp
---------------------

Project:   https://github.com/ggml-org/ggml and https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp
License:   MIT
Copyright: (c) 2023-2026 The ggml authors

Where this applies:

  * The GGUF file layout read by quintrit-format, including the metadata value types, the
    tensor info records, the alignment rule and the keys under "tokenizer.ggml.*", and the
    numeric ggml tensor type ids (F32, F16, Q8_0, BF16, TQ1_0, TQ2_0, I2_S).
  * The TQ1_0 and TQ2_0 ternary block layouts decoded by quintrit-format (block size, scale
    placement, base-3 digit order, 2-bit element order). The conformance tests re-implement
    the dequantizers `dequantize_row_tq1_0` and `dequantize_row_tq2_0` of ggml as references.
  * quintrit-runtime, module `ops`: the single-precision exponential, SiLU and SwiGLU
    vector routines follow the algorithm and polynomial coefficients of `ggml_v_expf`,
    `ggml_v_silu` and `ggml_vec_swiglu_f32`, and the half-precision dot product,
    multiply-add and scale routines follow `ggml_vec_dot_f16`, `ggml_vec_mad_f16` and
    `ggml_vec_scale_f16`, so that results are bit-identical to ggml.
  * quintrit-runtime, module `attention`: the online-softmax attention with a half-precision
    accumulator follows `ggml_compute_forward_flash_attn_ext_f16_one_chunk`, and the rotary
    position embedding cache follows `ggml_rope_cache_init`.
  * quintrit-runtime, module `config`: the choice of the beginning-of-sequence token follows
    the vocabulary loader of llama.cpp.

