2. BitNet (bitnet.cpp) and BitNet b1.58
---------------------------------------

Project:   https://github.com/microsoft/BitNet
License:   MIT
Copyright: (c) Microsoft Corporation.

Where this applies:

  * The I2_S ternary weight format (two bits per trit, four trits per byte, 128-weight
    blocks, one per-tensor scale) read by quintrit-format. The packer and unpacker for this
    layout (`pack_gguf_i2_s` and `unpack_gguf_i2_s`) reproduce the data layout of the
    reference kernels of bitnet.cpp.
  * The BitNet b1.58 transformer architecture implemented by quintrit-runtime (sub-layer
    normalization, squared ReLU feed-forward, tied embeddings) and the post-scaling
    convention of the integer matrix-vector product, which are implemented to give results
    identical to the reference runtime. The activation quantization to int8 follows the
    reference runtime.

  * The crate quintrit-bitnet: a Rust transcription of the 4-trit kernels of bitnet.cpp (the
    planar multiply-add kernels of `ggml-bitnet-mad.cpp`, the 32-row tiled lookup kernel and
    their data layouts), with a widening of the multiply-add kernel to AVX-512. It is a
    comparison baseline, is not published to crates.io and is not part of the C library or the
    Python package.

